# CASM Phase 12 WP68 Increment 7 trusted reference: casmarithfwd
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmarithfwd fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves
# CASM_PARSER_STMT_FORCE_ABS (parser.s:928-940) holds across a genuine
# two-pass real assembly for a forward-referenced NAMED CONSTANT combined
# with a WP68 operator -- the same property casmfa2p.ref.hex proved for a
# bare forward-referenced label (WP61 Increment 4), now one level removed
# through a new arithmetic operator. "LDA FWDCONST*2" must emit as 3-byte
# absolute ($AD lo hi), never shrink to 2-byte zero-page ($A5 lo), even
# though the computed value ($000A) would fit zero page if it were a
# literal.
#
# Source (.ORG $0010, load-bearing -- keeps CasmRelocatableMode static/0
# for the whole assembly; see the WP68 Increment 7 plan's Atomic Step 1
# audit for why this matters for a forward-referenced identifier):
#   LDA FWDCONST*2
#   FWDCONST = 5
#
# CasmPc starts at $0010. FWDCONST is not yet in the symbol table when
# "LDA FWDCONST*2" is first measured (Pass 1) -- a genuine forward
# reference. CASM_EXPR_FLAG_SYMBOL_DERIVED is set unconditionally the
# moment the resolver call returns (expr.s:318-320), regardless of whether
# the symbol itself resolved, and combineStatic's staticUnresolved path
# (expr.s) propagates it through the '*' application without evaluating
# the multiply (RESOLVED clear, no placeholder arithmetic). Pass 1 thus
# sizes "LDA FWDCONST*2" as 3-byte absolute without yet knowing FWDCONST's
# value or the product. Pass 2 -- which re-parses the statement from
# scratch, by which point FWDCONST is fully resolved to 5 via
# casmResolveConstants -- independently re-derives the identical FORCE_ABS
# classification (SYMBOL_DERIVED still set, now on a RESOLVED result) and
# commits the same 3-byte absolute opcode, now with the real computed
# value FWDCONST*2 = 5*2 = 10 = $000A.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   10 00              PRG load-address header ($0010, little-endian)
#   AD 0A 00           LDA $000A                    (absolute, FORCE_ABS)
#
# FWDCONST = 5 emits no bytes (a named-constant definition is a pure
# symbol-table entry, matching casmconst1.seq's own precedent).
#
# bytes: 5
# sha256: ed747101efeeb1af567f2b55a092f62cbd2d8e62c82ed0e70171701cc69a5373
# source_sha256: casmarithfwd.seq=9968fa789d2a0079772f74c39e7788954fbb264b9c1cad6b7461cd75343b93f9

10 00
AD 0A 00
